            "steps": "<ol><li>Get two pots and a measuring cup. In one pot pour 2 ounces of water, and in the other pour 6 ounces of milk.</li><li>Mash up 2.5 grams of fresh ginger (optional) with a mortar and pestle if you have one — a blender works too — and add it to the water.</li><li>Put the water and ginger on the stove over a simmer. Wait for it to start bubbling, then add ½ tsp of the chai powder and stir regularly.</li><li>Let the chai spices boil for a few minutes, then add 1 teaspoon of black tea powder. Keep stirring on simmer-medium heat until the tea-water thickens significantly — the longer you brew, the stronger the flavor.</li><li>After boiling the tea leaves for 1–2 minutes, add 6 ounces of the milk of your choice to the pot. We recommend a barista oat milk — they hold up better to heat.</li><li>Bring the chai to high heat and let the tea infuse into the milk over 2–3 minutes.</li><li>Strain, and ready to serve!</li></ol>"
